"""
AYC Portal — Application constants and configuration.
Imported by helpers.py, app.py, and every blueprint.
No Flask objects live here — plain Python only.
"""

import os
from dotenv import load_dotenv

# ── Instance directory (multi-tenant) ─────────────────────────────────────────
BASE_DIR     = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
INSTANCE_DIR = os.environ.get('INSTANCE_DIR', BASE_DIR)

# Load .env from the instance directory before anything reads os.environ
load_dotenv(os.path.join(INSTANCE_DIR, '.env'))

# ── Paths ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DATABASE     = os.path.join(INSTANCE_DIR, 'data', 'ayc.db')
UPLOAD_DIR   = os.path.join(INSTANCE_DIR, 'data', 'documents')
LOG_DIR      = os.path.join(INSTANCE_DIR, 'data', 'logs')
BRANDING_DIR = os.path.join(INSTANCE_DIR, 'data', 'branding')

# ── Version ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
APP_VERSION = 'v12.67'  # v12.67: audit fixes #4–#7 (16 July audit). (4) Import multi-session merge no longer drops the paid marker: a merged row carrying _payment_paid now records a whole-club membership payment on the TARGET member unless they already have a non-voided membership payment for the current period (guard means N paid rows for one person still create exactly one payment; voided and non-membership payments don't satisfy the guard). blueprints/admin.py. (5) Scoped users can now only CHANGE session assignments within their own sessions — /api/members/<id> PUT previously accepted any valid session (add) and a crafted payload could remove out-of-scope assignments; now added/removed sessions outside the user's scope → 403 ('You can only add or remove sessions within your own sessions'), matching the rule approvals already enforced. The check runs BEFORE set_member_sessions (replacing the write-then-rollback pattern) and mirrors its semantics — unknown names dropped, inactive-type assignments treated as preserved (v12.65) — to avoid false 403s. members.html edit modal: out-of-scope chips are now LOCKED (disabled, dimmed, tooltip) rather than toggleable; disabled checked inputs still serialise into the save payload so existing out-of-scope assignments round-trip unchanged. blueprints/members.py, templates/members.html. (6) Incident notifications: /api/mailshots/send with incident_note_id now validates every recipient against THAT member's contact emails (case-insensitive) and 400s on any outsider — previously any in-scope recipient set was accepted and the note stamped 'notified' even if no email reached that member's family; UI unaffected (it already pins the checklist). blueprints/communications.py. (7) Casual-skin attendance table capped at the 20 most recent rows with a 'Showing the 20 most recent of N' note — the endpoint returns up to 104 rows PER session since v12.62 (for the formal skin's per-session grid), which the casual flat table rendered in full (a 3-session long-standing member got a 300+ row table in the member card). Formal skin unchanged. templates/members.html. Verified: mirror tests for the payment guard (double-paid rows → one payment; voided/non-membership ignored), the scope-change matrix (out-of-scope add/remove 403, unchanged out-of-scope pass-through, junk-name drop, inactive preservation → no false 403, empty-set rule kept, in-scope swap OK), incident recipient intersection (case-insensitive own-contact pass, other-member reject, NULL/blank contacts ignored); py_compile clean; members.html Jinja + JS parse clean. blueprints/admin.py, blueprints/members.py, blueprints/communications.py, templates/members.html, config.py. # v12.66: audit fix #3 — import duplicate/merge matching can no longer target staff or silently merge onto archived members. admin._find_existing_member now (a) EXCLUDES staff records (LEFT JOIN member_types, COALESCE(registration_style,'') != 'staff') so a register row whose match fields collide with a staff member is never folded into (or skipped against) the staff record; (b) prefers a match whose status behaviour is 'active' (ORDER BY CASE) so a returning member matches their live record ahead of an archived duplicate; (c) returns the row (id, status, status_behaviour) instead of a bare id. Callers updated: the multi-session merge path adds a review warning when the only match is a non-active record ("combined into an existing member whose status is 'Left' — they will not appear on any register until their status is changed"), joined onto any phone-clash warning; the skip-duplicates reason names the existing record's status when it is not active, so the results screen explains why the "duplicate" is not on any register. Members with an unknown member_type slug still match (LEFT JOIN + COALESCE). AYC round-trip import deliberately unchanged — it imports staff as well, so a staff exclusion there would be wrong. Verified on a mirror schema: active preferred over staff + archived same-key rows; archived-only match found and flagged non-active; staff-only match returns None; all-blank identity never matches; NULL-postcode-matches-blank and unknown-slug behaviour preserved. blueprints/admin.py, config.py. # v12.65: two silent-data-loss fixes from the 16 July audit. (1) Session-type DELETE guard now counts assignments via the member_sessions junction (with the members.session echo as a defensive OR), not the echo column alone — members.session only holds the FIRST assigned session, so deleting a type that was anyone's second/third session reported 0 members and ON DELETE CASCADE then silently stripped those junction rows (a Tue+Thu member lost Thursday with no warning and their paid-coverage requirement quietly shrank). Error message now says the count includes non-first sessions. blueprints/calendar.py. (2) helpers.set_member_sessions now validates against ALL session types (active governs UI visibility, not data validity) AND preserves existing assignments to INACTIVE types that the caller omits — the edit modal only renders chips for active types, so editing anything on a member assigned to a deactivated session (e.g. a summer-only group) silently dropped that assignment on save; explicit inactive names are also accepted now, matching the import path (admin._apply_member_sessions already used all types). Verified on a mirror schema with foreign_keys ON: old guard misses junction-second-session + echo-only members (new counts both), cascade loss reproduced then blocked; set_member_sessions preserves inactive on an active-only payload, accepts explicit inactive, still drops unknown names, keeps echo = first by sort_order, idempotent on double-call. helpers.py, blueprints/calendar.py, config.py. # v12.64: fixed "Generate Term" only creating one session per weekday. api_calendar_bulk built target_weekdays as {weekday: session_name}, so when several session types share a day (e.g. multiple Saturday groups) each overwrote the last and only one per weekday was created (15 selected → ~9 in the calendar). Now maps {weekday: [session_names]} and inserts EVERY matching session on each date. term_sessions already has UNIQUE(session_date, session_type) so same-day different-type rows are allowed. Verified: 15 sessions across 7 weekdays over 2 weeks → all 15 types created (30 rows), all five Saturday groups present on each Saturday. blueprints/calendar.py, config.py. # v12.63: session-type colours + calendar overhaul. (1) session_types gains a colour column (hex; idempotent ALTER + fresh DDL + preserved in the weekday-nullable rebuild); helpers.get_session_types and the admin session-types API return an effective colour (admin-set, or a deterministic 12-colour palette fallback by id, so every screen is stable before a colour is chosen). Admin → Session Types gains a colour picker (add + edit) and a row swatch. (2) CALENDAR now colours each entry by its session type (pill filled with the type colour); status is shown by styling — Special gets a ★ + ring, Cancelled is struck through and faded. Legend rebuilt to list session-type swatches + the status styles. Colours are calendar-only for now (per Nik). (3) FIXED "can't create a Special session": the UI always sent status='special' but the backend only accepted 'extra' (→ 400), AND the weekday validation rejected any session added on a non-standard day. Now VALID_STATUSES uses 'special' (legacy 'extra' rows migrated at startup), and the weekday check is bypassed for Special sessions (the whole point of a special is an off-schedule day). (4) NEW calendar views: Month / Week / Day switcher with unified prev/Today/next nav; /api/calendar accepts a from/to date range for the week/day fetches. Verified: extra→special migration, from/to range query, palette/hex helpers, and the special-session weekday bypass. db.py, helpers.py, blueprints/calendar.py, templates/admin/session_types.html, templates/calendar.html, config.py. # v12.62: member card attendance tab (modern/formal skin) now shows one row PER SESSION instead of merging every session into a single dot strip. loadAttendanceHistory groups /api/attendance/history rows by session_type and renders an att-grid — each session is a labelled row (name + present/total) with its own horizontally-scrollable dot strip (att-row-scroll, nowrap), auto-scrolled to the most recent entry; a 15-session member gets 15 scannable rows. Overall present/absent + session count in the legend. Casual skin (table listing) unchanged. Backend: the history endpoint's global LIMIT 20 (which a multi-session member exhausted in ~2 sessions) is replaced by a ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY session_type ORDER BY session_date DESC) window keeping the most recent 104 (~2 years) PER session — bounded payload, real per-session history to scroll. SQLite 3.37 (sqlcipher3) supports window functions. templates/members.html, blueprints/attendance.py, config.py. # v12.61: register session field now shows the session the register is FOR, not the member's echo column. A multi-session member (e.g. Thea Brophy in Ballet + Saturday Group 4) appears on both registers but the 'session' field (when enabled as a show-on-attendance / show-on-print field) showed her echo column (first session, "Ballet") on BOTH. Fixed in all three register render paths to use the register's session context: register.html memberCard detailPairs (uses sess), print_register.html field_val macro (uses session_type global), and pages.py print_register_xlsx _field_value (uses session_type). Swept the rest of the system: members list/card already shows all sessions (v12.60), comms merge-field joins all sessions (v12.51), member detail/edit + dashboard tiles + export use the junction, approvals uses the chip picker — all correct. templates/register.html, templates/print_register.html, blueprints/pages.py, config.py. # v12.60: fixed multi-session members showing only ONE session on the member list/card when 'session' is enabled as a show-on-list / show-on-card field. renderFieldVal() rendered the system 'session' field from the single members.session echo column (member[column_name]); it now special-cases column_name=='session' to join the full member.sessions array (member_sessions junction, already returned by /api/members line ~174), falling back to the echo when the array is absent. The dedicated card subline was already correct; this was the field-config display path. templates/members.html only. # v12.59: fixed "Delete all members" (Admin → Maintenance) aborting with sqlcipher3 IntegrityError: FOREIGN KEY constraint failed. The DELETE FROM members ran while child rows still referenced it — session_notes.member_id has NO ON DELETE action (schema db.py ~L197), and the other member-child FKs only cascade with the pragma on. api_maintenance_clear_members now clears children first: it discovers every table with a FK pointing at members via PRAGMA foreign_key_list (so future member-linked tables are covered automatically) and unions a known list (attendance, dofe_participants, member_sessions, member_contacts, member_tags, member_field_values, member_flags, member_payments, session_notes) in case any lacks a formal FK; strictly per-member tables are full-wiped, then members. session_notes is special-cased — only member-linked rows (member_id IS NOT NULL) are deleted so general/club session notes survive; the deleted-note count + cleared tables are recorded in the audit log. Verified on a mirror schema with foreign_keys ON: old path reproduces the exact IntegrityError, new path clears members + all child rows and preserves the general note. # v12.58: import wizard multi-session support + configurable duplicate identity. (1) New "Multi-session register" toggle on the import preview step (chk-multi-session) sent as multi_session in the /api/admin/import/run payload. When on, rows that match the same person (per the configurable match fields, case-insensitively) are folded into ONE member: the first occurrence creates the member, later occurrences are merged via new admin._merge_member_row which unions the row's session onto the member's member_sessions (';'-joined through _apply_member_sessions), backfills a blank mobile/email/emergency-contact from the extra row, and FLAGS (never overwrites) a non-empty phone that disagrees as a warning. Matches this-run members first, then any pre-existing DB member (only when skip-duplicates is also on), so re-imports add sessions instead of duplicating. Response gains merged count + warnings[]; results screen shows a "combined into existing members" card and a review-warnings panel. (2) CONFIGURABLE duplicate key (per Nik — a fixed key was too fragile): new "Match duplicates on" checkbox group on the preview step, populated from the mapped fields (First Name, Surname, Date of Birth, Postcode, Mobile, Email), remembered browser-side (localStorage ayc-import-match-fields), sent as match_fields[]. The SAME field set drives BOTH the skip-duplicate check and the multi-session merge. Backend whitelists match_fields to real member columns and builds a dynamic lower(COALESCE(col,''))=? WHERE via new admin._find_existing_member (injection-safe; NULL treated as blank; an all-blank identity never matches). Skip-duplicate reason text names the fields used. (3) Bug fix (all modes): the old skip-duplicates check compared postcode = '' but stores empty postcode as NULL, so NULL <> '' let every no-postcode register row through as a fresh member — the new COALESCE-based check fixes this. Verified: real 131-row combined register collapses to 113 members (18 merged, 15 multi-session, 0 false conflicts) on first+surname; coarser/finer keys behave (surname-only → 99; two same-name different-DOB children merge on first+surname but stay separate once DOB is added); py_compile + JS check clean.  # v12.57: fixed approve/reject and Complete Register modals rendering below the fold on long lists — root cause was .page-content's page-enter animation (transform-based, shared.css) leaving a permanent CSS containing block for position:fixed descendants, so modal-overlay centred against the full scrollable content height instead of the viewport; base.html now clears the animation once it finishes (animationend + 400ms fallback), and resets it before the page-exit animation so nav transitions still play. Removed the now-redundant window.scrollTo(0,0) calls from approvals.html's openApproveModal/openRejectModal — they didn't address the real cause and are no longer needed.  # v12.56: incident→comms (client requirement 2) — a member-linked register note can be emailed to the member's parent/guardian from the Comms section, with a send receipt. (1) Schema: session_notes gains notified_at + notified_by (idempotent ALTERs + fresh-install DDL). (2) API: GET /api/comms/incidents (mailshots.send perm) lists member-linked notes newest-first — ?days window (default 30, clamped 1–365) or ?note_id for deep links; rows carry the member's contact emails (email holders only) and the notified receipt; session-scoped users only see notes from their sessions. POST /api/mailshots/send accepts incident_note_id — validated up front (exists, member-linked, in scope) and stamped + audit-logged (incident_notified, with recipient emails) only after ≥1 email actually sends; mailshot_log filter_criteria records the note id. (3) Comms UI: collapsible "Session Incidents" panel (last 30 days, pending count) with per-note Notify buttons; incident mode pins the recipient checklist to that member's contacts, pre-fills subject + FULL details body (per Nik's decision — staff review/edit before sending; nothing sends automatically), amber banner with cancel; previewRecipients no-ops in incident mode so filter changes can't clobber the pinned list; successful send exits the mode and refreshes the panel. ANY member-linked note type qualifies (Nik's decision), incl. General/Other. Deep link /communications?incident=<note_id>. Members with no contact email show a red 'No contact email on file' instead of a button. (4) Register: member-linked session-log notes gain a 'Notify parent/guardian' link (mailshots.send holders; 'Send again' once notified) plus a green '✉️ Notified <date>' badge; notes API returns notified_at/notified_by_name. Verified: incidents query scoping/member-linking, email-holder contact filtering, no-email path, receipt stamping; py_compile + JS + Jinja parse clean.  # v12.55: multi-session membership Phase D (final) — import/export, alert rules, echo retirement. (1) Import: 'session' column accepts a delimited list ("Tuesday; Thursday" — separators ; , / |), validated case-insensitively via new admin._apply_member_sessions which writes member_sessions + echo; unknown tokens reported as row warnings in the import errors list (member still imported); both the generic mapped import AND the AYC round-trip import covered, including session values arriving through the custom-field column path (falls back to reading the just-written members.session). (2) Export (CSV + XLSX): Session column emits every assigned session '; '-joined via ordered group_concat subquery — round-trips through the import parser losslessly; _export_where session filter matches via junction. (3) Alerts: applies_to_session rule targeting via junction; scoped alert counts via junction; ATTENDANCE RULES now evaluate the member's COMBINED timeline — last N completed registers across ALL assigned sessions, newest first, flagged only if they attended none of them (= disengaged from the club; a member who dropped Tuesday but attends Thursday is NOT flagged — per design discussion with Nik; per-session variant can be added as a rule option later). Attendance match is on (session_date, session_type) pairs. (4) members.session is now written-only (echo maintained by set_member_sessions/import/approvals for rollback safety): remaining reads are deliberate defensive fallbacks (comms merge-field COALESCE, alerts/members echo fallback when a member has no junction rows); permanent-delete audit logs the full sessions list. Verified: import parse (mixed case/separators/dupes/unknowns), export→import round-trip, combined-timeline alert matrix (attended-one-recent not flagged, stale-attendance flagged, single-session unchanged, insufficient-history skipped) all pass; py_compile clean.  # v12.54: fixed admin session dropdowns collapsing — members.html session filter and communications.html session picker branched on `not current_session` to decide scoped vs unscoped, but the register picker persists active_session even for admins (v12.41), so an admin who had used the register saw the members dropdown locked to that one session + Staff/Volunteers, and comms mailshots were silently locked to it. Both now branch on `not session_names` (empty = unscoped admin, always full dropdown; non-empty = scoped user, unchanged behaviour).  # v12.53: multi-session membership Phase C — per-session payments. (1) member_payments gains nullable session_type_id (idempotent ALTER + fresh-install DDL); NULL = whole-club payment covering every assigned session, which is the meaning of all pre-existing rows so nobody's paid status changes on upgrade. (2) Recording: payment modal gains a "Covers" picker — Whole club (default) or one of the member's assigned sessions only; POST/PUT validate session_type_id exists AND the member is assigned to it; PUT can move a payment between sessions or back to whole-club ('session_type_id' in data pattern, consistent with the v12.41 partial-PUT fix). (3) Paid semantics: paid_current now means FULLY covered (whole-club payment, or every assigned session covered by session payments); new paid_sessions[] lists covered sessions. /api/members computes coverage in Python from one batch query (replacing the paid_sub SQL join; paid=1/0 filter param applied post-coverage with the same staff exclusion). /api/members/<id>/payments returns session_name per row + paid_sessions + member_sessions; payments table gains a Covers column; period badge shows green Paid / amber "Paid n/m (sessions)" / red Unpaid. (4) Members list: paid badge + paid filter are session-context-aware — with a session selected they mean covered FOR THAT SESSION; on All Sessions fully-paid shows green, partial coverage shows an amber "Paid n/m" badge (tooltip lists sessions); new .badge-partpaid-f style. Verified: paid-matrix SQL test (Tuesday-only payment = paid on Tuesday/unpaid on Thursday; whole-club = paid everywhere; per-session ×2 = fully paid; voided + non-membership ignored) passes; py_compile + JS parse clean.  # v12.52: display screen follows the register's selected session — /display now accepts ?session=<name> (validated against session_types) as the highest-priority session source, ahead of the user's assigned session and the day-of-week fallback; the register's "Open display" button sets the param from the session picker at click time. Fixes: with multiple sessions, opening the display always showed the same session regardless of the register's dropdown. Everything on the display keys off the one currentSession value, so the members board, activities ticker and the display QR token are all session-correct.  # v12.51: multi-session membership Phase B — the most-used screens now read the member_sessions junction. (1) Register/attendance: member + staff register queries, absence-row generation at register completion, and attendance history scope all use the junction, so a Tue+Thu member appears on BOTH registers and can sign in to both on the same day (attendance rows were already per session+date, unchanged). (2) QR sign-in member search matches any assigned session. (3) Print register + register XLSX + register export (pages.py, 5 query sites) use the junction. (4) Approvals: approve accepts sessions_assigned[] (legacy session_assigned string still works); ALL assigned sessions must be inside a scoped approver's own scope; member/staff creation writes junction rows via set_member_sessions; staff portal-login creation grants user_sessions for every assigned session; pending_registrations.assigned_session deliberately stays a single name (the requested/first session) so pending-list scoping is unchanged; approvals.html gains the same .sess-chip checkbox picker as the members editor for member AND staff approvals. (5) Comms: recipient session filter + scope via junction with 'no sessions assigned = reachable by everyone' preserved (NOT EXISTS), DISTINCT email dedupe guarantees one email per member across N matching sessions; Session merge-field now renders all sessions comma-joined (COALESCE to echo). (6) Dashboard: per-session tiles count a member once in EACH of their sessions (junction GROUP BY), headline totals stay member-distinct, scoped headline/alert counts + per-session growth series via junction. (7) payments._member_in_scope and alerts api_member_flags scope checks switched to any-session intersection (delegate to helpers.member_in_scope). Remaining m.session readers are Phase D scope: alerts rule matching/counts (alerts.py 61/65/505) and admin export filter (admin.py 3619). Verified: junction register/comms/dashboard SQL behaviour tests (multi-session member on both registers, dedupe, per-session double-count vs distinct totals, merge-field join) all pass; all blueprints py_compile; members/approvals template JS parse-checked.  # v12.50: multi-session membership Phase A — members can belong to N sessions. (1) New member_sessions junction table (member_id, session_type_id, UNIQUE pair) mirroring user_sessions, with indexes. (2) Startup reconcile: set-based INSERT OR IGNORE seeds member_sessions from members.session on EVERY boot (idempotent + self-healing while approvals/import still write the old column; orphan members with blank/unknown session are logged). (3) members.session kept as read-only echo (first assigned session by sort_order) for not-yet-converted readers (register, comms, dashboard, alerts read it until Phases B–D); set_member_sessions() maintains the echo. (4) helpers: get_member_session_names, get_sessions_for_members (batch), set_member_sessions (validates against session_types, dedupes, echo sync), member_in_scope (any-session intersection with echo fallback). (5) members API: list/session filter + scope via EXISTS on junction; every member payload gains sessions[]; PUT accepts sessions[] (legacy single 'session' still accepted, converted); all six member-endpoint scope checks switched to intersection; scoped editors can't save a session set that removes the member from all their sessions. (6) members UI: edit modal session dropdown replaced with checkbox chips (.sess-chip, :has(:checked) styling); card subline lists all sessions ('Tuesday · Friday'); client-side session filter matches any assigned session. SQL logic verified by idempotency/intersection test run twice against fixture data. Phases B (register/QR/approvals/comms/dashboard), C (per-session payments), D (import/export/alerts + drop echo) to follow per AYC_MultiSession_Plan.docx.  # v12.43: mobile responsiveness pass (fixes shipped in the v12.42 tree; this bump documents them and cache-busts the CSS) — (1) .data-table mobile column-hiding (<768px) now exempts the last column, so Actions stays reachable on Manage Users / Comms templates; td gains overflow-wrap:anywhere for long emails (shared.css + skin-casual.css). (2) form controls (search-input, session-select, form-group inputs/selects/textareas, form-input) bump to 16px font below 768px to stop iOS Safari focus-zoom. (3) auto-fill card grids use minmax(min(Xpx,100%),1fr) so 260–330px minimums can't overflow narrow phones (members grid-f, documents, roles, member_types, settings, approvals, dashboard). (4) dashboard .dash-grid forced to 1 column below 768px (was repeat(2,1fr)) per Nik — stat cards and today-cards stack full-width. (5) session pill ellipsizes at 42vw <480px; toast spans viewport width <480px. (6) calendar day cells tightened <480px (58px cells, 8.5px pills) so the 7-column month stays usable. (7) horizontal-scroll wrappers on field_builder assigned-fields table, both admin payments tables, and the member-card payments table.  # v12.42: audit smaller-observations pass — (1) db.py ensure_tables seeding refactored from 9 per-section connections to one shared `seed` connection wrapped in try/finally (the payment-field migration previously leaked its connection on error); verified with a 13-check seed test run twice for idempotency. (2) session.permanent set at login so permanent_session_lifetime (8h) actually applies. (3) requirements.txt duplicate flask-wtf range dropped (pinned Flask-WTF==1.2.2 stays). (4) gunicorn timeout 60→120s for synchronous mailshot sends. (5) new helpers.client_ip() (X-Forwarded-For gated on TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS, default trust for the Caddy topology) used by login lockout, registration + QR + postcode rate limits and audit-log IPs — behind Caddy all users previously shared ONE rate bucket, so 10 failed logins by anyone locked everyone out and audit entries logged the proxy IP. (6) mailshot explicit recipients validated against the sender's scoped member contacts (endpoint previously accepted arbitrary addresses — open-relay risk). (7) members flag_rule_id join parameterised. (8) session-scope checks added to member tags GET and permanent delete. (9) helpers.club_slug(): all export/backup filenames now use the branded short name consistently.  # v12.41: audit fixes — (1) register session picker: admins are never locked to active_session and options are filtered server-side to the user's sessions; onSessionChange persists for admins too. (2) /admin/settings/import-history 500 fixed (duplicate session_types kwarg vs tpl_ctx). (3) XSS: register card data-name attribute now esc()'d. (4) session-type rename cascade extended to session_notes, quick_signin_tokens, alert_rules.applies_to_session, pending_registrations.assigned_session. (5) APScheduler guarded by flock so only one gunicorn worker runs the nightly alert check; RUN_SCHEDULER=0 disables. (6) payments PUT no longer wipes omitted payment_date/method_id/notes. (7) payment_types.is_membership flag replaces name='Membership' matching (members paid filter, member payments paid_current, import). (8) staff approval resolves the staff member-type slug instead of hardcoding 'staff'. (9) /api/postcode rate-limited 20/min/IP. (10) DB restore: connection closed before swap, WAL checkpoint before snapshot, stale -wal/-shm removed before copy. (11) session grants (role/permissions/session_names) re-synced from DB every 60s — role edits, session reassignments and deactivation now apply without re-login. (12) audit/calendar numeric query params validated (400 instead of 500).  # v12.40: register summary tiles (Signed In / Not Arrived / Signed Out) are now clickable filter views — keep their counts but filter the grid to that state so signing members out no longer means scrolling to the bottom; click the active tile again to show everyone. Default register sort changed to First Name. Both the active state filter and the sort order are persisted per user in localStorage (key ayc-register-<username>) so they survive refreshes, session changes and page navigation. (Members tab only; staff tab unchanged.)  # v12.39: filtered staff out of all remaining dashboard attendance counts — api_dashboard today_att (Today's Sessions headcount), and api_stat_trends att_by_type (Today's Sessions sparklines) + att_rows (Attendance last-session % and sparkline) now JOIN members→member_types and filter registration_style != 'staff', consistent with v12.38.  # v12.38: fixed the attendance trend chart to exclude staff — api_attendance_trend joins attendance→members→member_types so only the selected cohort is counted (previously counted members + staff); accepts ?view=members (default) or ?view=staff; dashboard trend card gains a Members/Staff pill toggle that switches view, retitles the card and rebuilds the chart; staff view with no data keeps the card visible.  # v12.37: replaced the print register's in-page Print button (which mis-rendered on some browsers — v12.36 image-wait attempt did not fix it) with an Export to Excel button. New /register/print.xlsx route builds an .xlsx mirroring the print layout: embedded logo header, title/subtitle, the member type's show_on_print fields, boolean YES/NO, and blank Tick on Arrival / Tick When Leaving columns plus 5 walk-in rows. Uses the resolved member-type slug (not hardcoded 'member'). Logo embedding needs Pillow (added to requirements) and degrades gracefully if absent. Printing is now via the browser menu / Cmd+P. Removed the now-unused printPage() from print_register.html (kept on register_export.html).  # v12.36: print register/export Print button now waits for all images (notably the cache-busted /branding/logo) to finish loading before calling window.print(). Printing mid-load made Chrome re-render the preview when the logo arrived seconds later, blanking the large fixed-layout table and the on-screen page; Cmd+P was unaffected because the logo had already settled. printPage() added to print_register.html and register_export.html with a single-print guard and 3s safety timeout.  # v12.35: removed remaining hardcoded 'member' slug fallbacks on write paths — member import and public registration now default to the club's primary active non-staff member type (first by sort_order) instead of 'member', and resolve unknown/blank slugs to it, so clubs with a renamed type slug (e.g. ara-members) no longer create orphaned members/registrations invisible to every mt.slug = m.member_type join.  # v12.34: print register now filters members by the resolved member-type slug instead of the hardcoded 'member' default (clubs with a renamed type slug, e.g. ara-members, were getting 0 rows on the printable register); guarded the v11.2 show_on_attendance data migration so it is skipped whenever any member field already has a Show On flag set — the UPDATE was not idempotent (rewrote show_on_card = MAX(card, detail), which fed back in and re-flipped show_on_attendance = 1 each startup), so every field was ending up on the attendance card.  # v12.33: approval modal — initial status picker; defaults Active, supports Provisional workflow  # v12.22: sticky footer — body flex column, page-content flex:1 + width:100%, app-footer margin-top removed. Footer now always at viewport bottom on short pages, natural scroll position on long pages. v12.21: search bar height — explicit height:44px on .search-input and .session-select in shared.css (formal light/dark + casual dark) and skin-casual.css (casual light). Previous padding-only approach had no effect because inter 14px + 1px border + box-sizing:border-box = 40px regardless of padding. v12.19: dashboard — zero-count card hiding; per-user layout prefs (drag-to-reorder, hide/restore cards, hide sections); global trends toggle; reset layout; localStorage keyed by username. v12.18: final sweep — register.html (7 hardcoded navy→token), members.html (badge colours→token). v12.15: display.html — drop Google Fonts CDN→vendor/fonts.css (CSP fix); add ?mode=light support via html.light-mode CSS override block (body bg #f1f5f9, navy text, white cards). v12.14: batch 7 — remaining admin sub-pages. attendance_settings: tokenize casual amber overrides (#fef3c7→var(--amber-bg), #fcd34d→color-mix, #78350f→var(--amber)), white→var(--cream) for qr-toggle-card, dual-render ⚠️ in safeguarding note. member_types: rgba box-shadow→color-mix(accent). smtp_profiles: #dc2626→var(--red). system_logs: outer border #1e293b→var(--border), dual-render ⚠️/🔴 level-btn icons. session_types/payments/staff_roles: clean.

